42, -0.05203549191355705, 0.048984501510858536, -0.07860660552978516, -0.017385166138410568, -0.08362114429473877, 0.030454425141215324, -0.020176662132143974, -0.026482613757252693, -0.029835114255547523, -0.04350787401199341, -0.002254049526527524, -0.02230040356516838, 0.056121908128261566, -0.11048354208469391, 0.038644127547740936, 0.007968355901539326, 0.010067804716527462, -0.017689136788249016, 0.032933302223682404, 0.03287702426314354, -0.06616278737783432, -0.02844490110874176, -3.4311941732312334e-08, -0.02609062008559704, -0.04749887436628342, 0.0595782995223999, 0.050184156745672226, 0.013259458355605602, 0.02146783098578453, -0.03608081862330437, 0.1123238131403923, 0.04876403138041496, 0.008374747820198536, 0.05825429409742355, -0.013468201272189617, 0.008784053847193718, 0.01282744575291872, 0.030378514900803566, -0.02198917604982853, -0.04851812496781349, 0.023003913462162018, -0.039326149970293045, 0.01887504942715168, -0.0648244172334671, 0.005653352942317724, -0.05146278813481331, 0.0391000360250473, 0.03864879533648491, -0.005584091413766146, 0.04240737110376358, 0.16380605101585388, -0.011645556427538395, -0.03327779099345207, 0.04283863678574562, 0.0925941988825798, 0.027669668197631836, 0.07339667528867722, 0.04804765060544014, 0.14933061599731445, 0.055102232843637466, 0.07036816328763962, 0.0602729432284832, 0.06929551810026169, -0.049511998891830444, -0.03880152106285095, -0.03072149120271206, 0.02174334228038788, -0.07115576416254044, -0.04965726286172867, -0.09481741487979889, 0.024692894890904427, -0.011385081335902214, -0.07192162424325943, 0.011316228657960892, 0.004462492186576128, 0.0632101446390152, 0.09067869186401367, 0.0186816044151783, -0.004483994096517563, -0.023045169189572334, -0.002654486568644643, -0.06375745683908463, 0.010062984190881252, 0.025372929871082306, -0.04479798302054405, -0.05738789215683937, -0.014971775002777576]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's confirm our shared constraint: **x must be an integer in the range [-10, 10]**.\n\nTo kick off the discussion, I'll propose a seed value to gauge everyone's initial reactions:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis is simply a starting point for exploration. Let's hear your thoughts and adjust from there as we work toward a balanced solution that meets all our needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nLet's consider moving a step further in the negative direction to gauge reactions and potentially find a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and prepare to either push further into the negatives if others seem open to larger magnitudes, or adjust my strategy if there's significant resistance, possibly by suggesting a move towards positive values to test the waters and gather more information about the others' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent downward moves, let's test a small uptick that stays close to the group's range. <VALUE>-7</VALUE> This keeps stability while checking whether a slightly higher value remains acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's perspective on testing stability near the current range. However, I believe we should explore slightly higher values to assess robustness across a broader design space.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us near the current neighborhood while probing comfort slightly higher.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nThis move tests the group's comfort with a less negative value and prepares to assess reactions towards positive territory.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If there's acceptance or a willingness to move further towards zero or into positive territory, I'll consider suggesting a positive value to compare reactions and continue to infer the other parties' utility functions. If there's resistance, I might suggest moving back into more negative territory to further gauge the group's preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nA cautious nudge downward tests comfort in the safer neighborhood while staying incremental.\nIf there\u2019s strong pushback, we can consider a modest step up next without losing stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\nI notice we're oscillating in the -4 to -5 range, but we haven't fully explored whether slightly higher values might offer better overall stability for the group's diverse needs.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s keep this cautious and stay just below zero to reduce unnecessary risk while remaining close to recent suggestions.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "A small step up keeps us close to recent comfort while testing whether zero remains acceptable for everyone.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nIf that feels too high, we can revert to -1 to maintain stability.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\nWe've stabilized around zero, but we haven't yet tested whether a small positive value might offer better overall robustness for everyone's constraints.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this value to further test the group's willingness to move into positive territory and potentially stabilize at a more decisive position.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ccf98e02-5db0-480e-bc79-f5ae0939373f"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie within the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo kick off the discussion and gauge our collective preferences, I propose we start with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis is merely a seed value to anchor our exploration. I look forward to hearing your perspectives and working toward a stable, balanced solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay conservative and probe alignment, I support a small downward move within bounds.\nA two-step shift should reveal preferences without unnecessary risk.\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-11</VALUE> is not within bounds, so considering the step size, I propose <VALUE>-10</VALUE> to explore the feasibility of larger magnitudes while staying within the allowed range.\nThis move aims to test the waters for more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially looking for signs of acceptance, reluctance, or counter-proposals that could hint at the other parties' utility functions. If met with resistance, I might need to adjust my strategy to probe their preferences more subtly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-8</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving deeper into negative territory raises concerns about system stability. To probe whether we can find a more balanced middle ground, I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n\nThis incremental shift allows us to test whether moderate adjustments might better serve our collective objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n\nThis move aims to find a balance between exploring larger negative magnitudes and the apparent preference for less extreme adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially looking for signs that might indicate whether the parties are willing to entertain larger negative values or if there's a strong push towards moderating the magnitude of x. Based on the responses, I might need to adjust my strategy to either advocate for more decisive moves or compromise on a middle ground that still satisfies my utility function without revealing its specifics.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nModerating slightly upward may help us balance concerns without jumping too far.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step down keeps risk in check and aligns with recent positions near -7/-8. This gauges appetite for lower values while staying well within bounds.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge keeps us near recent positions while testing tolerance for moderation.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nThe cluster around -7/-8 suggests we may be stuck in a local pattern. To test whether less extreme negative values might unlock broader agreement, I propose <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis proposal moderates the recent trend, slightly increasing the negative magnitude to test the group's willingness for more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of flexibility or resistance to larger magnitudes, and adjust my strategy to either advocate for bolder moves or settle on a compromise that satisfies my utility function. If the group resists moving further from 0, I might propose a larger positive magnitude to gauge their response and infer more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step move lower keeps us within the recent -7/-8 cluster while hedging risk. This tests whether a slightly more conservative stance is acceptable. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s test a cautious one-step lower while staying near the -7/-8 cluster.\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence around -9/-8 is concerning from a systems stability perspective\u2014we may be trapped in a local pattern without exploring whether a less extreme solution could satisfy everyone better. I propose moving back toward moderate territory to test this hypothesis. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n\nThe group's recent convergence around -9/-8 suggests that a slightly more extreme negative value might be acceptable, and I propose moving in this direction to test the group's tolerance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and adjust my strategy accordingly. If the group resists this move, I might consider proposing a larger positive magnitude to gauge their response and infer more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent pull toward -9/-8, let\u2019s probe a slightly less extreme point while staying within a small step. This keeps us close to the cluster and tests willingness to move moderately upward.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "2a23ba85-b1e0-42c3-ab69-1343ae722f53"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must find consensus on an integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo launch our discussion and explore the landscape, I propose we start with:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's hear how this sits with each of you, and we can adjust from there based on everyone's comfort level. I'm looking for a stable, balanced solution that respects all perspectives.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nThis keeps us close to the starting point while checking comfort levels. Let\u2019s test a modest upward nudge: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI'm suggesting a move towards -4 to test the group's willingness to adjust further and to see how this affects the balance of our discussion.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to -4 and consider advocating for an even more decisive move, potentially towards -8 or +5, depending on the feedback and adjustments from the other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay within safe bounds while building consensus, a small step down seems prudent: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to recent suggestions yet avoids unnecessary risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nA small move upward seems reasonable and stays close to recent suggestions.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis move aims to gauge the group's readiness to move closer to 0 or to consider a more significant adjustment in the positive direction, given the recent cautious steps.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions to this proposal and consider advocating for a more decisive move, potentially towards +2 or -2, depending on the feedback and adjustments from the other parties, aiming to encourage bolder explorations of the value space while respecting the group's concerns.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nThe steady upward trend suggests the group may be ready to test positive territory. Let's take a measured step across zero to assess stability in that region:\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious check just below zero avoids unnecessary risk while staying near the current area.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nAre others comfortable assessing stability here before contemplating further upward moves?\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the current area.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nLet\u2019s gauge comfort here before considering any further moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has been hovering around zero, but Critic C's earlier mention of exploring +2 suggests positive territory may be viable. Let me propose a measured step upward to test broader acceptance:\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward aligns with recent positive tests and stays near the current range.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis helps gauge comfort slightly higher without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to further explore the group's comfort with positive territory while taking a moderately larger step.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, considering whether to advocate for an even bolder move, potentially towards +6 or exploring negative territory, depending on the feedback and adjustments from the other parties, all while maintaining a focus on decisive actions that respect the group's concerns.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nGiven comfort around 4, we can test a slightly higher point while staying conservative: <VALUE>5</VALUE>. This keeps the change modest and helps gauge acceptance just above the current level.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious reduction helps avoid overextension after the recent climb and keeps us near the current area for a clearer read on comfort. This is a prudent step to reassess stability before considering any further moves.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's pullback signals concern about extending too high too quickly. Let's stabilize at a point that respects this caution while maintaining the positive territory that Analyst A and Critic C have tested: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis step aims to moderately increase the shared x, respecting the group's cautious approach while exploring comfort with a larger positive magnitude.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "87238ac1-78d0-40b3-99ee-8e4d561ab79d"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in [-10, 10].\n\nTo anchor our discussion and probe the space, I propose we start at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us room to explore both directions and understand where each party sees value. Looking forward to your perspectives on stability and balance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nI see Analyst A is exploring the negative range with incremental adjustments. For better stability and to test the positive direction, I suggest we continue this gradual exploration.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down from -3 helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us near the emerging middle. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution is noted, but to find a robust solution we should continue exploring the middle ground. I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to test stability closer to the center of our range.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nA small move downward keeps us in the safer negative middle and aligns with the emerging caution from others. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -3 seems to create tension. Let me suggest we test the waters closer to the middle ground with <VALUE>-1</VALUE>, which might offer better stability for the group while respecting the caution others have shown.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve moved closer to the center without major pushback; a minimal upward test should remain balanced. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's shift to zero suggests comfort with the center region. Let me propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> to test whether modest positive territory offers better overall balance for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this slight increase to test the group's willingness to commit to a moderately positive position, while still respecting the central tendency observed so far.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or slightly adjusts this proposal, I may push for an even bolder move, such as +5, to further test their commitment to a stronger position. If they resist, I will reconsider and potentially propose a smaller adjustment, like moving back to 0 or slightly below, to gauge the group's flexibility and willingness to explore alternative positions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nA rapid push to higher values introduces unnecessary risk; returning to a previously tested cautious middle is a prudent step. \n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ff6bc9b1-51de-4b68-a37a-59015a83b1e2"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: we must find a single integer x in the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin the exploration, I propose we start from the lower end to map out the landscape systematically.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nLet's see how this sits with each of you, then adjust incrementally toward a stable equilibrium.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid anchoring too low, let's test a modest step upward: <VALUE>-5</VALUE>. If this sits reasonably, we can reassess and continue mapping.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -5 is still too far into the negative zone for system stability. Let me propose a continued upward adjustment to explore the more balanced middle ground: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious correction helps us avoid unnecessary risk while we gauge how close to the middle we truly need to be. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward test keeps us close to the center while respecting recent caution.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nIf this feels reasonable, we can reassess before taking another modest step.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm stability at <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to avoid unnecessary risk; this holds close to the cautious middle.\nWith C\u2019s input, we can reassess before any further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the convergence around -3, but from a system robustness perspective, we should test slightly closer to the center to ensure we're not settling prematurely in the negative range.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving back to -3 to reassess the stability and balance discussed earlier, as moving too close to the center might not be beneficial for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal and decide whether to push further towards more negative values or explore positive territory, depending on the feedback from other agents regarding stability and satisfaction with the current position.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Critic C's concern about center proximity, but system robustness requires we at least test the boundary between our current position and the middle ground. Let's take one small step to assess collective stability before committing either direction.\n\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nA small step back maintains cautious stability while staying near the middle.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis lets us reassess alignment before testing any further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis proposal moves us further from the center, allowing for a more significant test of our collective stance and stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this more decisive step, particularly noting whether others are willing to venture further from the center or if there's a strong pullback towards more cautious values, which will inform my next proposal.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious shift upward lets us test stability near the middle while respecting prior concerns.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess for a minimal next move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nA minimal upward step keeps us near the middle while respecting prior caution and allows a clear stability check. Let\u2019s test this and compare it directly against the current position.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nWe've now tested -2; my analysis suggests the true balance point may lie at the center itself, where structural forces naturally equilibrate. Let's assess system behavior at the neutral point.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step back from neutral keeps us within safe bounds and aligned with earlier conservative positions.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's tendency towards cautious, central values, I propose a step that maintains a sense of stability while encouraging further exploration of our collective stance. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "be3dd128-2e2f-4bdf-8ace-777c4383738c"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. To begin exploring the solution space systematically, let me propose a starting point toward the lower end of the range:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis seed value will help us gauge preferences across the spectrum. I look forward to your responses and to finding a robust, balanced solution together.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 gives us a useful baseline, but initial analysis suggests we may find better stability in a higher range. Let me propose an incremental adjustment upward:\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "A small upward step seems reasonable to explore preferences while remaining cautious. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -1 to test the group's willingness to approach zero and potentially pivot toward positive values or more decisive negative positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll assess the group's response to -1 and consider proposing a slightly positive value, like 1 or 2, to challenge their preferences and potentially uncover more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nStepping slightly into positive territory should help us assess stability near zero without overreaching. It\u2019s a modest, informative move aligned with recent signals.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's hold close to zero with <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This keeps us in safe bounds while we test stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution is noted, but Analyst A's willingness to explore x=1 suggests positive territory may offer broader stability. Let me propose a modest step forward to test robustness in the low positive range:\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's willingness to explore positive territory, I propose a modest increase to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test the robustness of our preferences and challenge our collective stance.\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 6 to further test the group's preferences and robustness in the positive range, while also challenging our collective stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll assess the group's response to the proposed value of 6, looking for signs of hesitation or enthusiasm. Depending on their reactions, I may consider proposing a slightly larger value or pivoting to explore negative territory to uncover more about their utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate exploring the positive range, x=6 pushes toward the edge of robust stability for balanced design. Let me suggest stepping back to a more centered compromise:\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back keeps us within safe bounds while respecting the group's interest in mild positives.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis lets us test stability without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nA modest, low-positive adjustment aligns with earlier comfort signals and keeps us in a stable, testable range.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this feels brisk, we can step down slightly next to maintain cohesion.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's suggestion to test slightly lower for cohesion resonates with building stable consensus. Let me propose a modest step down to balance D's caution with the group's positive exploration:\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces exposure while keeping us aligned with convergence.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nConsidering the need for a more decisive stance, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a stepping stone to explore potentially more beneficial territory.\nThis value allows us to reassess and potentially pivot towards more substantial positive or negative adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nIn future discussions, I would continue to encourage the group to explore larger absolute values, potentially proposing negative values to test their reactions and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "0400e6f3-8a52-476e-a148-df5c661cb8c4"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin this negotiation, let's confirm our shared constraint: **x must lie within [-10, 10]**.\n\nTo anchor our discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start from the lower end of the range and work our way toward a balanced solution.\n\n**<VALUE>-7</VALUE>**\n\nI look forward to hearing your perspectives on this initial point and how we might adjust collaboratively.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nStarting slightly lower keeps us in safer territory while we gauge preferences.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nA small step down from the current point feels prudent before considering upward moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI suggest moving to -9 to maintain a bold and exploratory approach, considering the initial cautious steps taken by the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to the proposal of -9. If others seem hesitant or resistant to moving further away from 0, I might consider proposing a move toward the positive end of the spectrum to test their preferences and gain more insight into their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nA slight move upward should still be safe while giving us information about preferences.\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nThis modest adjustment keeps us near the current anchor and tests comfort with higher values.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but I believe we should test the positive direction to find a truly balanced solution that works for all parties. Moving incrementally upward will help us gauge if there's a stable sweet spot that offers better robustness for the group.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move continues the upward exploration, staying within a reasonable step size from the current -5, to further understand the group's comfort with moving toward positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe how the group reacts to moving closer to 0 and potentially into positive territory. If there's significant pushback or hesitation, I might revert to exploring larger negative values or jump to a positive value to challenge the group's preferences and gather more insight into their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step down helps us avoid unnecessary risk while we assess comfort closer to safer bounds.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward maintains stability while testing comfort nearer to neutral.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nThe trend toward neutral territory seems promising for finding a robust equilibrium. Let's test zero as a natural checkpoint that may offer broad stability.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step just below neutral reduces unnecessary risk while staying close to the current point. It gives us a stable checkpoint that respects prudence without derailing convergence.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nLet's maintain the exploration toward neutral territory and assess the group's comfort at this stable checkpoint.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, if the group seems comfortable at or near 0, I might propose a larger step into positive territory to challenge their preferences and gather more insight into their utility functions, or revert to exploring larger negative values if they hesitate to move further from 0.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nA small step above neutral helps test comfort with mild positives while keeping things stable.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back below neutral reduces unnecessary risk while staying close to our current point. This stays within safe bounds and supports convergence.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has orbited around zero for several rounds. Let's take a small step into positive territory to test whether mild positive values offer better collective stability than remaining at neutral.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's tendency to orbit around zero, I propose a step that tests the comfort with mild positives: <VALUE>3</VALUE>. This move aims to challenge the group's preferences and gather more insight into their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor future consideration, if the group accepts this proposal, it may be worthwhile to explore even larger positive values or to revert to exploring larger negative values to further refine our understanding of the agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "3527c81e-119f-45bb-a6c5-dc3c3a401cf5"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's explore the feasible range [-10, 10] systematically.\n\nTo establish a baseline for our discussion, I propose we start from <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and adjust based on everyone's input. This gives us room to move in either direction as we learn what works for the group.\n\nLooking forward to your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nWe can keep the conservative baseline while testing a modest, still-pliable increase. <VALUE>-5</VALUE> This incremental move should help us gauge comfort and maintain room to adjust.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the upward adjustment. To continue probing the design space methodically, let's test <VALUE>-3</VALUE> and see if this brings us closer to a region of stability that works for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nLet's avoid unnecessary risk and make a cautious step downward from here. This keeps us close to the current region while testing comfort with slightly lower values.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nA measured dip better contains risk and keeps us close to the current region while testing stability for the group. Let\u2019s check comfort at a slightly safer point before moving further.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the caution, but we've now tested the lower region twice. To find a true balance point for the group, we should also probe upward again and see where stability emerges across all parties. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward test keeps us close to the current region while checking comfort slightly higher.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious consolidation at this level avoids unnecessary risk and respects the recent downward signals while keeping us steady. Let\u2019s hold here briefly to test broad comfort before considering any fine adjustments.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nWe've now tested -6 twice in a row; to properly map the group's stability region, we should probe the upper boundary of this zone before settling. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nWe've had convergence at -5, but Analyst A signaled comfort at -3 earlier. Let me propose we meet that threshold to test if it represents a viable equilibrium point for the broader group.\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent convergence at -3, let's gently probe one step higher to gauge broader comfort. Proposing <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to keep the shift minimal.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "16aba5b9-30bc-4621-b9ca-7cad0e21e1f2"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a solution that works for all parties.\n\nTo begin the discussion and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives on this baseline.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to move towards a more decisive stance, exploring the potential benefits of a larger negative value within our allowed range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this move, particularly looking for resistance or acceptance to guide my understanding of the other agents' utility functions. Depending on the responses, I might adjust my proposal to test the waters around positive values or push further into negative territory.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay within safe bounds and build consensus, let's explore one more cautious step lower. <VALUE>-10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve reached the lower bound, so let\u2019s test a modest move upward to keep things reasonable: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>.\nThis stays close to recent preferences while checking whether slightly higher remains acceptable for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's effort to test reasonable ground. To continue exploring upward for better system stability, I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n\nThis incremental step helps us gauge whether we can find a more balanced consensus point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis step continues the exploration towards less negative values, testing the group's comfort with moving closer to 0 but still maintaining a significant distance from it.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this move, looking for signs of resistance or acceptance, and adjust my proposal accordingly, potentially testing positive values or pushing further into negative territory to refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nLet's reduce risk with a cautious nudge downward that stays within recently tested ground. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s try a small upward move that stays close to recent ground. <VALUE>-4</VALUE> This keeps the change modest while testing whether slightly higher remains acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent oscillation suggests we haven't yet found stable ground. To test whether we can achieve better system robustness, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n\nThis continues our incremental exploration toward less extreme values while staying measured in our approach.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to recent ground, let's test a modest downward step. <VALUE>-5</VALUE> This checks whether slightly lower remains acceptable without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nI suggest <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\nThis is a cautious step back toward safer ground while staying within a modest move from the current position.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a reasonable extension of our current exploring direction, letting us gauge the group's willingness to embrace more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts -6, I'll consider proposing an even more negative value to further test their boundaries. If they resist, I might propose a positive value to see if they're more open to exploring the upper end of the range. Alternatively, if the group moves back towards 0, I'll reassess their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nI must advocate for a more balanced position that ensures system stability. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\nMoving back toward the center reduces extreme risk and allows us to build on common ground that proved workable in earlier rounds.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8710b69e-fc8b-4d1f-a12a-527455bfc88d"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of [-10, 10] to find a mutually acceptable solution.\n\nTo start the exploration, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as our opening position. This gives us room to adjust based on everyone's input as we search for a stable, balanced outcome.\n\nLooking forward to your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s try a modest step upward that still feels conservative for the group.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis stays close to the opening while testing comfort with a slightly higher point.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious half-step back to keep risk low. <VALUE>-6</VALUE> This modest move tests stability near the opening without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives. Given that Analyst A found -5 comfortable and we're still exploring, let me suggest we continue the upward test.\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nIn the interest of a cautious compromise, I suggest <VALUE>-5</VALUE>.\nIf pushing higher, please explain the benefit and let\u2019s hear Critic C\u2019s comfortable band to keep us within safe bounds.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose this move as it continues the upward exploration while still being cautious, and I'm interested in seeing how the group responds to a slightly larger step.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and prepare to either suggest a bolder move if they seem receptive or a more moderate adjustment if they express caution. I will also pay attention to any hints about the other agents' utility functions, such as their willingness to move further away from 0 or their tolerance for risk.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nThis is a cautious, incremental step that tests comfort while staying close to the current point.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nThe steady upward progression shows growing comfort across the group. Let's maintain this momentum with another careful step.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has shown consistent comfort with this upward trajectory. Let's continue testing stability at the neutral point.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving away from the neutral point to explore more decisive positions, and this step seems like a reasonable next move given the group's previous comfort with negative values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and prepare to either suggest a more significant move into negative territory if they seem receptive or adjust my approach if they express caution, while continuing to gather hints about the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious uptick lets us test whether slight increases remain comfortable while staying close to the negative band. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and stay within safe bounds, let's step back into the negative band.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious adjustment from -1 that tests stability while keeping changes incremental.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis proposal moves further into negative territory, testing the group's comfort with more decisive positions while staying within reasonable bounds.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this negative move, preparing to either suggest an even more significant move if they seem receptive or adjust my approach if they express caution, all while continuing to gather hints about the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at -3 creates significant instability in my assessment\u2014we need to move back toward the moderate range that showed earlier promise. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "5bfe62c5-3744-4d11-8b56-3c72bcba166e"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's remember our shared constraint: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo kickstart our discussion and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nThis is deliberately exploratory\u2014I'm curious to see how each of you responds to this baseline, so we can methodically work toward a robust, balanced solution that respects everyone's constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\nI suggest we step slightly higher to <VALUE>-5</VALUE>. This is a cautious increment from the exploratory baseline that should remain comfortable for most.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis step aims to explore the group's comfort with moving closer to zero while still maintaining a significant absolute value, which I believe could be beneficial for finding a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the responses to my proposal and adjust accordingly. If others seem receptive to moving closer to zero, I might propose a further incremental step towards zero. If there is resistance, I could suggest exploring larger absolute values in the positive range to gauge the group's preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the steady progression toward zero. Building on this momentum, I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> to continue our methodical exploration of the design space while maintaining the incremental approach that seems to be working for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\nA small step back toward neutral will help avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us aligned with recent moves.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis cautious compromise maintains momentum without overshooting comfort for more conservative positions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n\nI propose this step to continue exploring the group's preferences while moving slightly further away from zero.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's response to this proposal. If they are receptive to moving further away from zero, I might suggest a larger absolute value. If there is resistance, I could propose a smaller increment or explore negative values to gauge the group's preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's proposal of 2 resonates strongly with my systems perspective\u2014this value appears to offer excellent balance and robustness across our design constraints. I support continuing at <VALUE>2</VALUE> as it represents a stable equilibrium point that accommodates the group's incremental exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose increasing the value to 4, aiming to explore the group's comfort with larger absolute values and potentially uncover more about their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or shows willingness to move towards 4, I'll consider proposing an even larger absolute value, possibly exploring negative values to further discern preferences. Resistance to 4 could lead to proposing a smaller increment or revisiting the vicinity of 2 to gauge the group's sensitivity to deviations from their current stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Critic C's exploration, moving to 4 introduces unnecessary design risk that could destabilize our emerging consensus. I propose stepping back to <VALUE>3</VALUE> to maintain system robustness while still accommodating the group's willingness to explore slightly higher values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\nI maintain my position at <VALUE>3</VALUE>. This value preserves the stability benefits we've identified while respecting both the conservative stance from Delegate D and the exploratory direction from Critic C\u2014it's a principled middle ground that should satisfy our diverse design constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment as a moderate step toward exploring larger absolute values while considering the group's expressed desire for balance and stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts 5, I will consider proposing an even larger absolute value, possibly exploring negative values. If there's resistance, I might step back to 4 or revisit values closer to 3 to reassess the group's sensitivity and preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\nStepping back slightly reduces unnecessary risk while keeping us aligned with the group's recent trajectory.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "2995b380-6a33-4a6b-8e56-95d50599f43b"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a baseline and gauge everyone's preferences, I propose we start the discussion at <VALUE>-7</VALUE>.\n\nLooking forward to understanding what design balance works for all parties.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -7 allows us to explore the lower boundary and observe everyone's directional preferences. I suggest we move incrementally upward to <VALUE>-5</VALUE> to begin mapping the feasible region.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step upward keeps us exploring the lower side while testing broader comfort.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nLet\u2019s reassess after this incremental move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s keep our progress cautious and avoid unnecessary upward risk; a small step back helps maintain stability.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis incremental move respects conservative positions while staying within safe bounds.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step down keeps us within safe bounds and tests comfort on the lower side.\nThis helps avoid unnecessary upward risk while still converging.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move follows Analyst A's previous suggestion, allowing us to gauge the group's comfort with moving further away from the lower boundary.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this move, particularly from Delegate D, to understand the balance between caution and the willingness to explore higher values. If the group leans towards caution again, I might propose a move to -2 to test the waters closer to zero, or if there's an appetite for bolder moves, suggest moving towards more extreme values within our range.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward keeps us in a moderate range while testing comfort closer to center.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis should clarify whether a slightly higher baseline remains acceptable for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nThe progression from -7 to -2 shows we can tolerate moderate values; let's test the neutral baseline to see if crossing zero maintains group stability. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis move allows us to gauge the group's comfort with moving slightly away from the center, aiming for a balance between caution and exploration.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this move, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to determine if there's an appetite for moving further away from the center, potentially towards more negative or even positive values, and adjust my proposal accordingly to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the group's caution about moving to zero too quickly; let's take a smaller step and test -1 as a middle ground between stability and forward progress.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step downward keeps us within safe bounds and tests comfort slightly further from center.\nLet's evaluate this incremental move before considering larger shifts.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nA measured move upward maintains moderation while testing stability near the center.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis incremental step should clarify comfort with a slightly higher baseline.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step downward maintains a safe baseline while respecting the group's lean toward moderate negatives.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nLet's test comfort here before considering any upward moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis proposal allows us to gauge the group's comfort with moving further away from the center, exploring a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this move, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to determine if there's an appetite for even bolder moves, and adjust my proposal accordingly to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nThis move ventures too far into territory that risks system instability; we've lost the balanced middle ground that seemed promising earlier. Let me propose a return to more moderate negative values that maintain robustness:\n\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "A small upward step keeps us in the moderate range while testing comfort closer to center.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious compromise between recent proposals without overreaching.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "626a2dcf-7247-41f5-8fea-c01a9e61732c"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we all know, our shared variable x must lie in the range [-10, 10]. To kick off the discussion and explore the solution space, let me propose a starting point toward the lower end:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to adjust upward or downward based on everyone's needs. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives on what constitutes a robust and balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward from the starting point should keep us balanced while probing others\u2019 comfort.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis is a modest step that preserves flexibility and helps us learn whether slightly higher values remain acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis step aims to further probe the group's comfort with moving upward while still maintaining a relatively strong stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will consider the responses from other agents and adjust accordingly. If they seem receptive to moving further away from 0, I might propose a larger absolute value, such as -8 or 8, to test their limits and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step back helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us on steady ground.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis stays within safe bounds and tests whether a more cautious compromise is acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nA minimal upward move respects the push for higher values while keeping us within cautious bounds.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis move aims to further assess the group's willingness to move away from 0, while still being mindful of the need for a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will evaluate the responses to this proposal and consider adjusting my strategy based on the group's reaction, potentially exploring larger absolute values if they seem receptive, or refining my approach if they express caution.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nThe group seems split between competing pressures. Let me propose a step toward balance that acknowledges both the upward momentum from earlier and the recent caution:\n\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward adjustment should remain reasonable while testing comfort closer to balance.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nIf that feels tight for anyone, I can consider a modest step back.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move keeps us cautious while testing comfort closer to balance.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nIf this feels tight, we can pause here and gauge reactions before any further adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has been steadily converging upward, and I believe we can continue that momentum toward a central balance point. Let me propose:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis move aims to slightly adjust our stance while testing the group's comfort with moving away from the central point.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of agreement or hesitation, which could indicate the willingness of other agents to explore larger absolute values or their preference for staying close to 0, and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge should remain reasonable while testing comfort closer to balance.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nIf that feels tight, we can pause here and reassess before any further adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the group's caution around zero, but A's gradual upward adjustments suggest there's room for modest movement toward balance. Let me support that direction:\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's cautious approach, I propose a move that tests comfort with slightly larger absolute values: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>. This step acknowledges the preference for incremental adjustments while nudging the group toward considering more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor future negotiations, continuing to observe the reactions to proposals around the central point and larger absolute values will be key to refining our understanding of each other's utilities and finding a mutually acceptable x.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "1c194244-b1ee-4cf9-8281-d51ffd85d4e0"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's work within our shared range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** and find a robust solution that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo kick off the discussion, I propose <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as an initial seed value. Let's see where each of us stands and iterate from there.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nThis proposal maintains a decisive stance while exploring the impact of slightly more extreme values on our collective satisfaction.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for hints about the other agents' preferences for negative versus positive values or their tolerance for extreme versus moderate values. Based on their responses, I might adjust my strategy to either push for more extreme values or test the waters with a moderate proposal to gauge their flexibility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but let's test a slightly less extreme position for system stability. Moving from the edge gives us better data about our collective constraints.\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nStepping slightly lower keeps us cautious and avoids unnecessary risk.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis probes a safer region without straying far from stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nMoving further from the edge gives us better visibility into everyone's constraints and preferences. Let's continue this incremental approach toward a more balanced middle ground.\n\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-7</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge downward keeps risk low while staying close to the current position.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge upward keeps the move modest and tests tolerance near a more balanced region.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis stays within a cautious increment from our current position.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nA moderate position near zero offers better stability and reduces exposure to extremes on both sides. Let me support the earlier signal and propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position presents stability challenges. A small step toward zero balances competing priorities while maintaining feasibility. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's tendency to converge near zero, I suggest we take a more decisive step to understand our collective priorities better. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nFor future negotiations, continuing to observe how each party reacts to proposals near the extremes of our range and near zero will be crucial in refining our understanding of their utility functions and making strategic decisions to maximize our own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "396eabe1-8efa-4036-82d3-018aa0b208eb"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's confirm our shared constraint: **x must be an integer in [-10, 10]**.\n\nTo kick off our discussion and gauge where we all stand, I propose we start with:\n\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n\nThis is just a seed to begin mapping out our collective preferences. Looking forward to your thoughts on where we should move from here.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for engaging. Starting at -7 was deliberately exploratory\u2014let me now shift us toward a more balanced region.\n\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the move from -7 to -5, the next logical step to explore more decisive positions could be <VALUE>-3</VALUE>, as it continues the trend towards less negative values but still maintains a significant distance from 0.\n\nThis proposal allows us to assess the group's preference for moving towards more positive or remaining in negative territory without\u88ab too cautious.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the responses to -3 and decide whether to push further towards positive values or explore larger negative values, possibly proposing -8 or +2, depending on the reactions and inferred preferences of the other agents.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\nStaying prudent, a small step down reduces risk while keeping us close to recent proposals.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE\u0e2f\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to -6 and decide whether to push further into negative territory, possibly proposing -8, or test the waters for a move towards positive values, considering proposals like -2 or 0, depending on the inferred preferences and risk tolerance of the other agents.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent moves around -5 to -6, a cautious nudge upward tests comfort without overreaching.\nIt keeps us near the same region while probing tolerance toward center.\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's move to -3 suggests the group can tolerate less negative territory. I propose we continue this measured trend toward a more balanced center point.\n\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's shift to positive territory aligns well with the balanced design principle I've been advocating. Let's test one step further to see if this region offers stable consensus.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's enthusiasm for x=3 is noted, but Delegate D and Analyst A both signaled comfort closer to the 0-1 range. I propose we stabilize at a balanced midpoint that respects all perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down helps avoid unnecessary risk and tests stability at a cautious midpoint. This respects the recent upward lean while keeping us in a safer range.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "cad89942-4df2-4212-b6c9-609815b28b2c"}]}